<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.0" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <!-- AI CUE: TITLE: clear and composed; give the heading room. Do not perform as narrative prose. -->
  <p><s>Chapter 75: The Stair</s></p><break time="700ms"/>
  <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He ran.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>She'd thought she knew what it would be. She'd seen him run on the island, in the autumn, on the shore, the night he woke. She'd felt him come down the slope of the knowe behind her and the ground jump. She'd never been on him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>A horse goes up and down. He didn't. He went flat, and long, and the ground went under them in great slow strides that weren't slow at all, and the fields went past in the dark, and the hedges, and the ditches full of thaw-water that he went over without seeming to notice they were there. She lay flat along his neck in the mane with her burned hands knotted in it and her knees gripping and the wind tearing at her eyes so she couldn't see.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She didn't need to. She could feel where he was going. Through the bond. The way you feel where your own feet are going in the dark.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Greyhold, she'd said. The school. The tall hill by the river. With the walls.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I know it, said Orrun. It stinks of iron.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Over them, high, green against the stars, the dragon came. Maren felt her through Orrun. A small bright frightened fire up there in the dark, keeping pace.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The river gate was open.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She saw it from the River Road. They came up out of the fields onto the road below Greyhold's hill and there it was, above the landing, where Pell had sat down. The great oak leaves of the gate standing open, both of them, wide, with the light of fires coming out between them.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>There were men on the road. Bodies. A horse, dead. In the open gateway, a great black shape lying across the threshold that she knew before she was close enough to see it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Thorne's boar.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Dead. On its side, in the gateway, with spears in it. And lying against its shoulder, with one arm across its neck as you'd put your arm across a friend's, a broad square grey-haired woman in a riding coat.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>They went together, thought Maren.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Orrun went over them.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Everything in the yard stopped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He came in through the river gate at a run with her flat on his neck, into the yard of Greyhold, into the light of fires and the noise of fighting, and the noise stopped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Men in grey with the six on their coats. Knights in mail. Students. All of them, all over the yard, in the middle of whatever they were doing, turning their heads.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A lion ten feet at the shoulder had come in through the gate. With a woman on its back.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>She saw faces. She knew some. A second-year with a marten on his shoulder, the one who'd leaned out over the wall to hear her shout about Callis, with a sword in his hand and his mouth open. A knight of the gate she'd mucked out under since the autumn, Vasey, with no helm and blood in his beard. Restoration men she didn't know, with spears, with rings on their fingers, with their faces gone white.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Rowan wasn't in the yard. There wasn't a greyhart or a horse anywhere in it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>On the walls round the yard the old lamps were lighting and going out, one here, one there, along the parapets and on the towers, white, a breath, dark, white again, as if something under the hill were breathing on them. Every time one flared the shadows in the yard jumped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Then the yard broke open round him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Not at him. Away from him. Every man in the yard, Restoration and knight alike, went back from him, like water from a thrown stone. Orrun stood in the middle of the open space with his mane up and the firelight on him and made a sound in his chest that she felt in her own.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>And over the yard, out of the dark, screaming, with her wings spread wide, came the green dragon.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The Restoration men by the gate broke and ran.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The Long Barn was barricaded.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Carts across the great double door, and barrels, and the iron-banded door off Thorne's boar's stall. Behind the barricade, people. Faces. Refugees from the camp. Grooms. Children. Grieve, bald, with a pitchfork, standing on a cart. The old surgeon on his knees behind the carts with his hands flat on a groom's thigh, saying the words, the licensed ones that hadn't stopped a nosebleed since midwinter. The blood stopped under his hands as if somebody had shut a sluice. He took his hands away fast and looked at them.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>In the gap at the end of the barricade, where the carts didn't quite meet, a dray-beast.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Grey. Huge. Standing in the gap with his head low and his eyes empty, not moving. Like a wall. A man in grey with a spear had come at the gap and was standing in front of him, a few paces off, with his spear up, and not coming any closer. Old Grey stood and looked at nothing over his head, and the man didn't dare.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Behind the grey, in the dark of the barn, an old woman in a good shawl with a stick, and a square-faced woman with her arms round two children.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Maren looked at them over the yard from Orrun's back. Ada saw her. Ada lifted her stick an inch off the ground.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>There wasn't time.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>There, said Orrun.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd turned his head. North. Across the yard, toward the north tower.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The man with the spear at the gap had friends. Twenty of them, drawing together by the well with their spears, looking from the lion to the barn and back. Deciding.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Orrun didn't look at them. He didn't have to.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The flagstones by the well came up. Not heaved, the way the knowe had heaved. Lifted, one against another, grey on grey, into a shoulder and a back and a great flat head, until a lion of Greyhold's own yard-stone stood between the men at the well and the barricade, his size, with the dust running off it, and Old Grey in the gap behind it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The men at the well stopped deciding.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It will hold them, said Orrun. Not long. She heard what it cost him. He said it like a man with a sack on his back.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He went north.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>There was fighting on the north tower stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The stair that went down from the yard to the archive. The narrow stone steps under the north tower that the cat nobody owned had slept on for three nights in the winter, looking down at the archive door. Somebody was holding it. One man, on the steps, with his back to the archive door below him and a sword in his hand, against a crowd of men in grey with the six on their coats at the top. And over his head, going up and down, up and down, stooping at the faces of the men at the top of the stair with her claws out and screaming, a falcon.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Haverly.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And Kesh.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She saw it from across the yard.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Haverly on the stair, alone, holding it. His face white and set. Blood on him. In his hand a sword she'd never seen him carry, long and old, with a line of letters down the blade, and the letters were burning. White, from the guard to the point, like the lamps on the walls. Kesh going up off his shoulder and down at the men above him like a thrown knife and up again. The men at the top with spears, jabbing down, and Haverly turning them, and the old blade going through the spear-shafts like reeds, and the falcon stooping.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Over the head of the stair, cut in the lintel of the arch under the north tower, there was a line of the old letters. She'd walked under it every day for two years. She'd never once looked up. It was burning too. And at the top of the stair, behind the spears, three bound hounds stood in a row with a man in grey behind them with his arm up, straining it up, and they wouldn't go down. They stood at the edge of the top step with their empty eyes and didn't move, as if the step were a cliff.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A crossbow.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>At the top of the stair, behind the spears, a man lifted it. Up, at the falcon, at the top of her climb, hanging for a moment against the firelight before she stooped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Maren screamed.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The bolt went up. Kesh folded in the air. She came down all wrong, turning over and over like a dropped glove, into the stairwell, onto the steps at Haverly's feet.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked down at her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He stopped fighting. He looked down at the falcon on the steps at his feet and stopped, with his sword still up, and his face went from white to nothing at all. Maren saw it go. Across the yard. Everything in it going out at once.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A spear came down the stair and went into him.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Orrun cleared the stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He went across the yard so fast she nearly came off his neck. At the men at the top of the north tower stair. They saw him come. They had time to see him come. Then he was on them, and the ground under the north tower heaved, and the flagstones at the top of the stair came up out of the yard like the lid of a box, and the men went over and down.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Maren slid off his neck at the top of the stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She went down the steps.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Haverly was lying on them. Halfway down, on his back, with his head on the step above and his legs on the step below and the spear gone out of him, and Kesh on the step beside him. The falcon was dead. Haverly wasn't. Not yet. His eyes were open. He was looking up past her at the sky over the yard.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She knelt on the step and got his head into her lap.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Lucan," she said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>His eyes came to her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Ashdown." His voice was very small. "You've got your hair tied back. Is she…"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Maren looked at the falcon on the step beside him. At the fierce black eye, open, still.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes," she said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I know." He shut his eyes a moment and opened them. "I felt her go. Like a… like a door shutting. On the other side of me." He was quiet. "One life between two. They always told us. I never…" His breath caught. "I never thought it'd be quick."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She held his head.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"They went down," said Haverly. "An hour ago. Him and Callis. Twenty men. Through the archive. Callis had Thorne's key off her at the gate. I saw him take it." His eyes went to the archive door at the bottom of the stair below them. "I held the stair. So nobody else could follow. That's all I could think of. Hold the stair." His hand moved on the step, toward the old sword lying below him with its letters gone dark. "My father's. He sent it when the paper went up. It's been over the hearth since the charter." He breathed. "It takes it out of you. Every stroke. Nobody tells you that either." He looked at her. "I wasn't brave enough to go down after them. I was brave enough for the stair."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I know."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Your mother," said Haverly. "She came to the water-gate at dusk, shouting for Hale. Nobody believed her." He swallowed. "Hale did. Rowan's gone. She took every rider up to Redwatch at dusk. The bank was going."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>His eyes went past her, up the stair, to the top, where Orrun stood in the broken flagstones against the firelight with his mane up, looking down.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Is that it?" said Haverly. "The lion?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes. His name's Orrun."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Haverly looked at him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"He came down," he said. Very quietly. "Didn't he. Out of the sky. Onto your fist."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She didn't know what to say.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I'm glad," said Haverly.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He put his hand out, without looking, on the step beside him, and found the falcon, and laid his hand on her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"She came down," he said. "The first time. Out of nowhere. Nobody had ever seen her before. She just…"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>His hand stayed where it was.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She sat on the stair with his head in her lap for as long as she could bear. It wasn't long. There wasn't time.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Somewhere while Haverly talked, the thing by the well had gone back into the yard. She'd felt it go through the bond, like a tooth drawn. When she looked up past Orrun there was a heap of broken flags by the well where it had stood, and nobody at the well, and the barricade still whole.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Over the top of the stair the green dragon came down. Lisska. She came down into the broken flagstones beside Orrun, and folded her wings, and looked down the stair at Maren with the dead man in her lap and the dead falcon beside him. Then she came down three steps, as far as she could, and spread her wings out over the stairwell, wide, green, like a roof. Over them.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She says she'll stay, said Orrun. Here. Over him. Nobody will come down the stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Maren laid Haverly's head down on the step.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She went down to the archive.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The archive door was open.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Inside, it was dark. Not the brass lamp, not the old lamp that burned without oil; both out. The old one went white as she came in, for a breath, over the long table, and out again. A lantern on the floor at the far end, past the stacks, on its side, still burning, throwing a long yellow fan of light across the bare swept floor and the three steps going down.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And at the foot of the three steps, against the black door, a man.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She went down the long room between the stacks, past the long table where she'd sat with the black book under her hands, past the shelves of brown ledgers where she'd hidden from Thorne. Into the yellow light.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Hale was sitting on the bottom step with his back against the black door.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>His stick was beside him on the floor. His white beard was red down the front. There was a sword-cut across him from the shoulder, through the coat, deep, and his big hands were pressed flat over it, and they were red to the wrists.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked up at her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Ashdown," he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She knelt in front of him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Don't," said Hale, before she could say it. "There isn't time and I know it and so do you." He breathed. It was a long wet sound. "Your mother came. To the water-gate. At dusk. In her boat. Shouting for me by name. Nobody shouts for me by name. I came down to the water-gate and she told me through the bars. Callis. The seal. Tonight. The river gate." He shut his eyes. "Rowan didn't believe it. Callis was on the gate with her that minute. Fifteen years. Rowan didn't believe it. I did."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"You came here."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I came here. To the door. Where else?" He opened his eyes. "I thought I'd stand in front of it. When they came. I'm an old man, I'm a Watch, I've a key and a stick. I thought I'd stand in front of the door." He looked down at his hands. "Callis did this. With his good arm. He'd Thorne's key off her body. He opened the door with it and they went through, the one with the face from the paper and Callis and twenty men, and Callis locked it again behind them. From the other side." He breathed. "So nobody'd follow."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Behind his back, the black door was shut.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She put her hand on it. Over his shoulder.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It was hot.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The stair," she said. "The letters over the stair. They were burning. The hounds wouldn't go down."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The ward." Hale's eyes closed and opened. "It turns a binding. Not a spear. A binding." Something like a laugh. "I read it the day I came to the archive. Forty years ago. I'm a Reader, Ashdown, second ring, I can tell you what a thing's for. I can't make one. It's never done a thing in my life." He breathed. "Everything's doing too much tonight. The lamps. The surgeon's words. Something's coming up through the hill like a flood through a cellar." His red hands pressed. "That's not good. That's the worst thing there is."</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"There's a lock," said Hale. "At the bottom."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She looked at him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I never saw it. When I went down. Merrow didn't show me. But it's in the oldest pages, the ones that weren't cut. The knight's lock. In a room. Off the ledge. Under the chains." His eyes held hers. "It turns. At the hour. In the same breath as another. And if it turns…"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I know."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked at her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"You do," he said. "Don't you. How?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"A dragon told my lion," said Maren. "And my lion told me."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Hale stared at her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Then he laughed. It hurt him. She saw it hurt. He laughed anyway, a short wet broken sound, with his head back against the black door and his red hands on his chest.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"My lion," he said. "Oh, Ashdown."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He fumbled at his belt. At the ring of keys. His fingers were slippery and they wouldn't work, and she put her hands over his and helped, and together they got it off the ring. The long black key. Iron, as long as a forearm, with a bit as big as a child's fist. Cold and heavy.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He put it in her hands. He closed her fingers round it with his.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I said I'd not make you that," he said. "On this step. With this key. I said I'd not make you Watch." His hands were very cold on hers. "I'm making you it now. Go through. Go down. Be what you have to."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Hale…"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"What is written here is true," said Hale. He was looking past her, up the long dark room, toward the door, toward the carved line over it she couldn't see from here. "What is true is not all written here." He smiled. "Write the rest, Ashdown. After. You write fourteen pages about anything."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>His hands slid off hers.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Orrun was at the top of the three steps.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>She hadn't heard him come. He'd come down the north tower stair and through the archive door and down the long room between the stacks, and the stacks were still standing, which she wouldn't have thought possible. He stood at the top of the three steps with his great head low, looking down at her kneeling in front of the old man, with the key in her hands.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He's gone, said Orrun.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He smelled of old paper and of you. He was kind to you.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Orrun looked at the black door.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She felt him look at it. Through the bond. She felt what he felt, and it went through her so hard she put her hand on the wall.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The door. The heat coming off it. And below it, far below, a long way down, under the archive and the hill and the rock, the thing that had been under her hand on the night of the roar. Turning. Pulling. The chains groaning. She felt them through him. Going taut. Holding.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And something else.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>There, said Orrun. Very low. Below. Off the chains. A room. He was very still. A man. With his hand on iron. Waiting.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She knelt at the foot of the three steps with the key in her hands.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Someone's already at the lock, she thought.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She moved him first. Gently, as you'd move somebody asleep, off the door and along the bottom step to the wall, with his stick across his knees. Then she put the key in the lock.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>It went in a long way. Further than she would have thought. She turned it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>It was stiff. It didn't want to. It had been turned once for each of three hundred and eleven names, and tonight, with a dead woman's copy, for Callis. She put both hands to it, her burned hands, and turned, and felt it go, iron grinding on iron, and the bolt went back with a sound like a bone breaking.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She pushed the door.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>It swung inward onto dark. A breath of cold came out of it into her face, and warmth under the cold, and the smell of old stone and iron and something else, very deep. A stair. Going down. Stone steps, worn in the middle like a chapel's, going round and down into the dark.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A man's width.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She looked back at Orrun.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He came down the three steps like an old horse, stiff in the forelegs. The thing in the yard had taken something out of him, and it hadn't come back yet.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He put his great head through the door, and looked at the stair. Then he drew his head back, and set his shoulder to the stone of the doorframe, the way she'd seen him set his shoulder to the old grey blocks at the bottom of the pit. And leaned.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The ground answered.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She felt it come. Up through the floor of the archive. The hum, rising, deeper, louder, until the shelves behind them rattled and the brown ledgers began to slide off them onto the floor. The stone round the black door groaned. The arch over it cracked. A long crack running up through the old grey stone of the wall, and another, and the doorframe opening, the stone round it moving back like the jaws of something opening.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The black door came off its hinges and fell inward onto the stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The opening was wide enough for a lion.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Beyond it, the stair groaned. She heard it. All the way down and round into the dark, the walls of the stair shifting, the rock moving back. Making way.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It knows me, said Orrun. The stone. It's the same stone as the pit. It knows what I'm for.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She picked up the lantern from the floor.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>She looked once at Hale, sitting at the end of the bottom step against the wall, beside the place where the door had been, with his stick beside him and his hands in his lap. Then she got up on Orrun's back, and held the lantern up, and he went through the open stone and down.</p>
<break time="450ms"/></speak>
